## 3. Global Data Quality Validation

A continuous quality assessment (QA) framework was embedded throughout the pipeline to systematically monitor the data transformation process and verify the elimination of technical biases.

### 3.1 Feature Reproducibility Improvement

The distribution of relative standard deviations (RSD) across pooled QC samples was evaluated to confirm the enhancement of technical precision.

![**Feature RSD Distribution Grid**](assets/01_QC_Sample_RSD_Dashboard.svg){.full-width-image}

### 3.2 Global Variance Alignment and Batch Effect Mitigation

Principal Component Analysis (PCA) was performed to visualize the global variance projection. The spatial aggregation of pooled QC samples in the corrected space corroborates the successful removal of systematic instrument artifacts and the preservation of authentic biological variance.

![**PCA Variance Projection Grid**](assets/02_PCA_Scatter_Dashboard.svg){.full-width-image}

### 3.3 Systemic Sample Coherence

To ensure global sample coherence, pooled QC correlation profiles were tracked dynamically.

